::ENG2_U05_L07_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Audience: school leaders. Which revision best polishes this sentence? "The library is a good thing for kids."{
~A. The library is awesome for kids.#Incorrect. Awesome is too informal and kids is less precise than students.
=B. The library provides students with a supervised academic space after school.#Correct. This revision is formal, precise, and fits school leaders as the audience.
~C. The library thing is good.#Incorrect. This remains vague and informal.
~D. I really like the library.#Incorrect. This is personal and does not address the audience's needs.
}

::ENG2_U05_L07_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.V.03] Which word has the most formal connotation for a school proposal?{
~A. cool#Incorrect. Cool is informal.
~B. awesome#Incorrect. Awesome is casual.
~C. neat#Incorrect. Neat is informal and vague.
=D. beneficial#Correct. Beneficial has a formal, positive connotation that fits a proposal.
}

::ENG2_U05_L07_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence uses standard English correctly?{
=A. Students cannot focus well in noisy hallways.#Correct. Well correctly describes how students focus.
~B. Students cannot focus good in noisy hallways.#Incorrect. Good should be well.
~C. Students waits for late buses after school.#Incorrect. Students requires wait, not waits.
~D. Students waiting hallway loud.#Incorrect. This is not a complete clear sentence.
}

::ENG2_U05_L07_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.V.02] Which word belongs to the same word family as revise?{
~A. visible#Incorrect. Visible is not part of the revise word family.
~B. visited#Incorrect. Visited is unrelated in this context.
=C. revision#Correct. Revision is the noun form connected to revise.
~D. vision#Incorrect. Vision may share letters but does not mean changing writing.
}

::ENG2_U05_L07_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which explanation best describes an audience-focused polish choice?{
~A. I changed the sentence because longer sentences are always better.#Incorrect. Length alone does not create polish.
=B. I replaced "kids" with "students who wait for late buses" because the audience needs a precise student group.#Correct. This explanation names the revision and why it helps the audience.
~C. I used random big words so the sentence sounds harder.#Incorrect. Precise words must fit the meaning.
~D. I deleted the claim because feedback means starting over.#Incorrect. Revision should improve the draft, not automatically remove the claim.
}
